# star_wars_2025_pro 0.84 - Spike 3 (64-bit ARM): drafted by s3port.py (PAD-1287) from the Spike 3 port star_wars_elg-1.10.port (star_wars_elg 1.10).
# Functions paired across the two titles: 9108 of 18297 reference functions (7431 anchored by vtable slots and strings, 362 through calls that line up, the rest grown through calls); half of them line up 100% or better.
# Written: what the reference port carries that is the FRAMEWORK's (each site's function at least 75% alike its
# reference's, each global and offset read at the lined-up instruction, the engines' layouts re-read off this program's
# own code); the switch lines from this program's own device table. The reference game's own content (shows, lamps,
# callouts, scenes, held coils, its modes) is not this title's: written as comments, for its own port.
# Switch ids MEASURED (PAD-1291): the game does not number its switches by their rank in the device table here - it
# numbers Right target after every other playfield switch (83, rank 61) and each switch after it one lower - so the
# switch lines are written from a census on the rig (proofs/swcensus.sh -> proofs/titles/star_wars_2025_pro-0.84.switch_ids,
# s3port.py --switch-ids): 27 switches sent their id; the slingshots, pop bumpers and drop target opto sent no hit.
# Emulator-proven 2026-11-15 (PAD-1291) on the Spike 3 rig (s3proof.sh, slots 240-242, hidden, muted; prebuilt
# mode64.so): the runtime took this port (29 sites, 27 shots, the Insider gate, 4 events, both switch_hit sites); CLOCK
# TEST started on the third Right target hit, scored 6 shots through the game's score_add (+21,000,000; score
# 13,500,090 -> 37,721,210) and ended when its 25 s ran out. MB TEST served 3 balls through the game's serve and ended at
# one ball; SAVE TEST's 15 s save served the drain inside it back and the drain after it ended the ball (SAVE CONTROL:
# its first drain); a stack no mode waited out the game's own centre-ramp multiball and started after the drain to one.
# Program sha1 2c9070fbd10913ecb3a25d93a7fc5cc2eea74bde (games/star_wars_2025_pro/game). Lamps, shows, screens, clips,
# callouts and the game's mode books are this title's own work.

game           star_wars_2025_pro
version        0.84

